1228 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This study applies Brubaker\047s \0502006\051 concept of \042groupness\042 to examine how shared experiences\054 rather than racial categorization\054 enabled belonging among students at Topaz High School\054 which operated within the Central Utah War Relocation Center and was attended primarily by Japanese American incarcerees\056 Drawing on oral histories\054 correspondence records\054 and other archival materials\054 this research found that students at an internment camp high school developed a sense of identity and community \050groupness\051 that transcended racial categorizations\056 In addition\054 the study found that historical memory preserves groupness over time as white students are included in the process of collective memory\056)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 1229 0 R
     /Pg 1212 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

